Feature: Outcome-Driven Experience Protocol for Accelerating Team Alignment and Delivery
  As a cross-functional software squad
  I want to rapidly align our work around high-value user and customer outcomes  
  So that every work output measurably advances business and customer value

  Background:
    Given a cross-functional software squad exists with PM, Engineering, and UX members
    And the squad has been assigned a high-visibility project
    And there are multiple stakeholder requests creating context-switching challenges
    And leadership demands faster delivery with measurable business value

  @protocol-validation @jtbd-opportunity-scoring
  Scenario: Successfully execute complete outcome alignment protocol
    Given the squad has access to user and customer insights
    And JTBD opportunity scoring methodology is available
    When the squad executes the accelerating delivery protocol
    Then all squad members can articulate the #1 JTBD and why it wins
    And a clear, measurable outcome statement is defined with consensus
    And all squad work is reorganized to align directly with the chosen outcome
    And greater than 90% of team work is aligned to the outcome
    And cycle time to outcome alignment is less than 5 days
    And team clarity/alignment score is greater than 8/10
    And reduction in waste approaches zero percent

  @real-world-example @sales-dashboard
  Scenario: Sales dashboard project with drifting priorities  
    Given a squad is building an internal dashboard for sales organization
    And managers across the company are requesting new features
    And teams are struggling with context-switching and drifting priorities
    When the squad applies the outcome alignment protocol
    Then they identify "Help sales leaders get accurate pipeline insights in real-time" as top JTBD
    And the JTBD has an Opportunity Score of 13 (critical unmet need)
    And they define the outcome as "95% of sales users can answer their top 3 pipeline questions in under 30 seconds"
    And all features are mapped against this outcome
    And management requests not tied to the outcome are deferred
    And the squad delivers highest business value with rapid user adoption

  @protocol-metrics @manager-dashboard
  Scenario: Track protocol success metrics for management visibility
    Given the outcome alignment protocol is in progress
    When managers review protocol metrics
    Then they can see percentage of team work aligned to outcome (target >90%)
    And they can see cycle time to outcome alignment (target <5 days)
    And they can see team clarity/alignment score via NPS (target >8/10)
    And they can see reduction in waste percentage (target approaching zero)
    And they can see measurable business/customer impact metrics
    And all metrics are updated weekly during protocol execution

  @cross-reference-validation @object-model-v4
  Scenario: Validate Object Model v4 cross-references are maintained
    Given the outcome alignment protocol is being executed
    When protocol tasks are completed
    Then every task/action is explicitly mapped to a measurable user or customer outcome
    And only top Opportunity Score JTBDs are in focus with lower-value items parked
    And success metrics are defined, tracked, and visible for leadership and team
    And all backlog/work outputs trace directly to outcome with unmapped items paused
    And BDD, Issue, and Outcome mappings are complete and up to date
    And "Did we actually deliver value?" validation is greenlit by all team members

  @anti-pattern @feature-drift
  Scenario: Prevent feature drift and scope creep during execution
    Given the squad has aligned on a single, measurable outcome
    And new feature requests are being submitted by stakeholders
    When requests are evaluated against the outcome alignment protocol
    Then requests that don't enable the chosen outcome are reframed or parked
    And management requests are reviewed for direct ties to the outcome goal
    And anything not directly supporting the outcome is deferred with clear rationale
    And the squad maintains focus on delivering the highest business value outcome
    And stakeholders understand what will and won't unlock the business result
